Ava (Docs): FYI I opened a PR to 1) replace legacy `cursor` examples, 2) add a concise pagination example using page tokens, and 3) standardize streaming snippets across py/ts/go. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/900

Leo (SDK): Happy to update TS+Go. Want to preserve backwards compat where possible. Do we want to recommend `page_token` + `page_size` over `cursor`?

Ava (Docs): Yes — recommend `page_token` (server-issued opaque token) in pagination examples. Add a short migration note: "If you relied on `cursor`, switch to `page_token` or streaming iterators depending on your flow." Put migration note in /docs/guides/pagination.

Jin (DevEx): For Python add both sync and async snippets and show how retry config is applied via client settings. Example async streaming pattern I'd suggest:
```py
async with client.responses.stream(model="rwd-large", input="List todos") as s:
    async for chunk in s:
        print(chunk.output_text, end="")
```
And a pagination example using page tokens:
```py
resp = client.responses.list_items(model="rwd-search", page_size=50)
while True:
    for item in resp.items:
        print(item.id)
    if not resp.next_page_token:
        break
    resp = client.responses.list_items(model="rwd-search", page_size=50, page_token=resp.next_page_token)
```
Add a one-liner showing retry config:
```py
client = Client(config={"retry": {"max_attempts": 4, "backoff": "exponential"}})
```

Leo (SDK): TS streaming example draft:
```ts
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'rwd-large', input: 'Summarize' });
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  process.stdout.write(chunk.output_text);
}
// client.config.retry defaults to { maxAttempts: 3, backoff: 'exponential' }
```
And TS pagination example with pageToken:
```ts
let res = await client.responses.listItems({ model: 'rwd-search', pageSize: 100 });
while (true) {
  res.items.forEach(i => console.log(i.id));
  if (!res.nextPageToken) break;
  res = await client.responses.listItems({ model: 'rwd-search', pageSize: 100, pageToken: res.nextPageToken });
}
```

Leo (SDK): Go snippet (stream + pagination):
```go
stream, err := client.Responses.Stream(ctx, api.StreamRequest{Model: "rwd-large", Input: "Summarize"})
if err != nil { log.Fatal(err) }
for stream.Next() {
  chunk := stream.Value()
  fmt.Print(chunk.OutputText)
}

// pagination
res, _ := client.Responses.ListItems(ctx, api.ListRequest{Model: "rwd-search", PageSize: 100})
for {
  for _, it := range res.Items {
    fmt.Println(it.Id)
  }
  if res.NextPageToken == "" { break }
  res, _ = client.Responses.ListItems(ctx, api.ListRequest{Model: "rwd-search", PageSize: 100, PageToken: res.NextPageToken})
}
```

Priya (Docs): Please add a short "Limitations" callout on the streaming page about quantized tiny models (e.g., rwd-tiny-q) not supporting low-latency streaming + KV-cache. Also include a brief note on best-effort ordering for partially retried chunks.

docs-ci-bot: link-checker found 2 issues: 1) broken anchor on /docs/guides/pagination (#old-cursor-example) and 2) unresolved relative link in /docs/sdks/go-examples.md -> ../reference/clients (404).

Ava (Docs): I'll fix the anchors and the relative link. We should also add a docs style note: prefer stable anchors and avoid inline repo links that may move.

Leo (SDK): Will remove `cursor: null` from all examples and run the link-checker locally. Branch: docs/pagination-page-token-900. Ill push TS+Go changes tonight and tag @Jin @Priya for review.

Jin (DevEx): I'll add a tiny regression test in snippets-ci that runs the streaming example and asserts that chunks include `output_text`. Also will validate the pagination flow returns `nextPageToken` when there are more pages.

Priya (Docs): I'll add the migration blurb and the limitations note, and patch the broken anchor.

Ava (Docs): OK looks like plan. Once CI green we'll merge. If the snippets test fails, we'll revert the doc change and iterate. Thanks all :thumbsup:
